# Sync the list, the folders INBOX, Next, Later, and Archive, both
# ways between Fastmail and Dovecot. Any other folder of the account
# stays on Fastmail. mbsync is an IMAP client of each, so it never
# opens the maildir. The folders come from Fastmail: one missing on
# Dovecot is created there, and none is ever created on Fastmail.
#
# New messages, flag changes, and moves travel both ways. Nothing is
# ever expunged or removed on either side: a message expunged on one
# side is only marked \Deleted on the other, so Fastmail keeps every
# message ever posted.

IMAPAccount fastmail
Host imap.fastmail.com
Port 993
TLSType IMAPS
UserCmd "sed -n 1p /data/secrets/mail-creds"
PassCmd "sed -n 2p /data/secrets/mail-creds"

IMAPStore fastmail
Account fastmail

# Dovecot on loopback, with no TLS. mbsync sends a password in the
# clear only over a mechanism named here.
IMAPAccount lab-mail
Host 127.0.0.1
Port 2143
TLSType None
AuthMechs LOGIN
User mbsync
PassCmd "cat /data/secrets/mbsync-imap"

IMAPStore lab-mail
Account lab-mail

Channel list
Far :fastmail:
Near :lab-mail:
Patterns INBOX Next Later Archive
Sync All
Create Near
Expunge None
Remove None
CopyArrivalDate yes
SyncState /data/mail/mbsync/
